# Private working dir — NEVER commit (error logs, benchmarks, probes)
# (covers the former per-file .private/* and .private/**/bin|obj rules)
.private/

# proptest-regressions/ is deliberately NOT listed here (issue #67).
# When a property test fails, proptest saves the shrunk input that broke it.
# Committing those files turns each found bug into a permanent, reproducible
# regression case that reruns on every machine and in CI; ignoring them would
# discard the minimal case as soon as anyone cleaned their working tree.
# The absence of an entry below is intentional — please do not "fix" it.
#
# Most of the saved cases came from deliberately mutating the codecs to check
# the tests actually bite, not from bugs found in passing code. They are worth
# keeping anyway: each one is the exact input that broke a specific guard, so
# if that guard is ever removed again the failure surfaces on the first case
# instead of waiting for random generation to rediscover it.
